@security
Feature: Tests d'attaque automatisés de l'application timesheet (Gauntlt)

  Background:
    Given "curl" is installed
    And "nmap" is installed
    And the default aruba timeout is 60 seconds
    And the following profile:
      | name     | value     |
      | hostname | localhost |

  Scenario: L'application répond et est en bonne santé
    When I launch a "curl" attack with:
      """
      curl -s http://<hostname>:18082/timesheet-devops/actuator/health
      """
    Then the output should contain "UP"

  Scenario: L'endpoint sensible /actuator/env n'est pas exposé
    When I launch a "curl" attack with:
      """
      curl -s -o /dev/null -w %{http_code} http://<hostname>:18082/timesheet-devops/actuator/env
      """
    Then the output should contain "404"

  Scenario: Le heapdump de la JVM n'est pas téléchargeable
    When I launch a "curl" attack with:
      """
      curl -s -o /dev/null -w %{http_code} http://<hostname>:18082/timesheet-devops/actuator/heapdump
      """
    Then the output should contain "404"

  Scenario: Les pages d'erreur ne divulguent pas de stacktrace
    When I launch a "curl" attack with:
      """
      curl -s http://<hostname>:18082/timesheet-devops/page-inexistante
      """
    Then the output should not contain "Exception"
    And the output should not contain "at org.springframework"

  Scenario: Aucun en-tête ne divulgue la technologie du serveur
    When I launch a "curl" attack with:
      """
      curl -s -I http://<hostname>:18082/timesheet-devops/actuator/health
      """
    Then the output should not contain "X-Powered-By"

  Scenario: La base MySQL n'est pas exposée sur l'hôte
    When I launch an "nmap" attack with:
      """
      nmap -Pn -p 3306 <hostname>
      """
    Then the output should not match /3306.tcp\s+open/
